<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/9th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Angers (851)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/851">851</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angers">Angers</a> was agreed in 851 between the West Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> and the Breton ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erispoe">Erispoe</a> after the Breton victory at Jengland. Charles recognised Erispoe as king and granted him the counties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rennes">Rennes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nantes">Nantes</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pays-de-retz">Pays de Retz</a> in return for his allegiance, fixing frontiers that Brittany largely kept throughout the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>.</p></div>
